IMPORT prelude

-- Asian Development Bank Act 1966 (Singapore) -- the Government's subscription limits (s 4) and how sums owed to the Bank may be paid
-- (s 5(2)); the Companies Act 1967 not applying to the Bank or its securities (s 10); and the parts of Chapter VIII of the Agreement
-- that s 9 gives the force of law, as a person dealing with the Bank meets them: who may sue the Bank and where (Article 50(1), (2)),
-- seizure of its property (Articles 50(3), 51), the immunities of its personnel (Article 55), taxation of the Bank, of its staff's
-- salaries and of its securities (Article 56) with the s 9(1) proviso, and waiver (Article 58).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ADBA1966.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The body carries no amendment
-- annotations; the Legislative History (not part of the Act) lists as its latest amending Act the Statutes (Miscellaneous
-- Amendments) Act 1991 (Act 11 of 1991, commencement 30 November 1991), followed by the 2011 Revised Edition.
-- The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS in the deposit is out of step by one line (it numbers "1." blank and "2. Short title"); the BODY's
-- numbering (s 1 short title ... s 11 rules) is followed here.
-- The Schedule reproduces Articles 48 to 56 and 58; Article 57 is shown only as a row of dots and is not in the deposit.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0156 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For a person, the answer is mostly the Schedule: whether they can sue the Bank, whether its officials can
-- be sued, whether their Bank salary or Bank bond interest can be taxed. Not encoded: ratification (s 3), the Consolidated Fund
-- charges beyond s 5(2) (ss 5(1), 6, 7, 8), the Minister's powers to amend the Schedule and make rules (ss 9(2), 11), Articles 48, 49,
-- 52, 53 and 54 (stated in comments only), and the Agreement itself beyond the Schedule (not deposited).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Asian Development Bank Act 1966 -- immunities and subscription`

§§ `4 -- the Government's subscription`

-- s 4: the Minister may subscribe "(a) to shares of the original authorised capital stock of the Bank ... to such amount as will not
-- exceed US$5 million"; (b) to a proportion of an increase under Article 5(2); (c) to an increase requested by the Government under
-- Article 5(3): "Provided that the subscription of Singapore shall not be increased, except with the approval signified by resolution
-- of Parliament, so that its total subscription exceeds the sum of US$10 million."
-- Amounts are in US$ millions.
GIVEN `original subscription in US$ millions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the original subscription is within s 4(a)` IF
    `original subscription in US$ millions` AT MOST 5

GIVEN `total subscription in US$ millions` IS A NUMBER, `Parliament has approved by resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the total subscription is authorised` IF
        `total subscription in US$ millions` AT MOST 10
    OR  `Parliament has approved by resolution`

§§ `5(2) -- how sums charged for the Bank may be paid`

-- s 5(2): "All sums charged on the Consolidated Fund under this section may be paid in gold or United States dollars or in local
-- currency."
DECLARE Medium IS ONE OF
    `gold`
    `United States dollars`
    `local currency`
    `euros`
    `Japanese yen`

GIVEN `the medium` IS A Medium
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sum may be paid in it` IF
    CONSIDER `the medium`
    WHEN `gold` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `United States dollars` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `local currency` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `10 -- the Companies Act does not apply`

-- s 10: "The Bank shall be deemed not to be a corporation within the meaning of the Companies Act 1967; and the provisions of that Act
-- shall not accordingly apply to the Bank or to the issue by the Bank of any shares, debentures, bonds, notes or other securities."
GIVEN `the issuer is the Bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Companies Act 1967 applies to the issue` IF
    NOT `the issuer is the Bank`

§§ `Schedule, Article 50(1), (2) and Article 58 -- suing the Bank`

-- Art 49: the Bank has full juridical personality and capacity to contract, hold property and "institute legal proceedings".
-- Art 50(1): "The Bank shall enjoy immunity from every form of legal process, except in cases arising out of or in connection with the
-- exercise of its powers to borrow money, to guarantee obligations, or to buy and sell or underwrite the sale of securities", in which
-- cases actions may be brought "in a court of competent jurisdiction in the territory of a country in which the Bank has its principal
-- or a branch office, or has appointed an agent for the purpose of accepting service or notice of process, or has issued or guaranteed
-- securities".
-- Art 50(2): notwithstanding (1), "no action shall be brought against the Bank by any member, or by any agency or instrumentality of a
-- member, or by any entity or person directly or indirectly acting for or deriving claims from a member".
-- Art 58: "The Bank at its discretion may waive any of the privileges, immunities and exemptions conferred under this Chapter".
-- INFERENCE: a waiver lifts the Art 50(1) immunity (and with it the venue condition, which is the condition of the exception); the
-- Art 50(2) bar on members is worded as a bar on actions, not as an immunity, so it is treated here as not waivable. The text does
-- not settle either point.
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a claim on the Bank's borrowing`
    `a claim on a Bank guarantee`
    `a claim on the Bank's buying, selling or underwriting of securities`
    `a supplier's claim for the price of goods`
    `an employee's claim for wages`
    `a claim for personal injury on Bank premises`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim falls within the Article 50(1) exception` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a claim on the Bank's borrowing` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a claim on a Bank guarantee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a claim on the Bank's buying, selling or underwriting of securities` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim,
      `the claimant is or derives from a member` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Bank has an office, agent or securities in that country` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Bank has waived its immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action may be brought against the Bank` IF
        (NOT `the claimant is or derives from a member`)
    AND (    `the Bank has waived its immunity`
         OR  (`the claim falls within the Article 50(1) exception` `the claim` AND `the Bank has an office, agent or securities in that country`))

§§ `Schedule, Articles 50(3) and 51 -- seizing the Bank's property`

-- Art 50(3): property and assets of the Bank "shall, wheresoever located and by whomsoever held, be immune from all forms of seizure,
-- attachment or execution before the delivery of final judgment against the Bank".
-- Art 51: they "shall be immune from search, requisition, confiscation, expropriation or any other form of taking or foreclosure by
-- executive or legislative action".
-- Art 52 (archives inviolable), Art 53 (assets free from restrictions, controls and moratoria "to the extent necessary"), Art 54
-- (communications treated no less favourably than other members') are not encoded.
GIVEN `final judgment has been delivered against the Bank` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the taking is by executive or legislative action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Bank's property may be seized` IF
        `final judgment has been delivered against the Bank`
    AND (NOT `the taking is by executive or legislative action`)

§§ `Schedule, Article 55 -- Bank personnel`

-- Art 55: "All Governors, Directors, alternates, officers and employees of the Bank, including experts performing missions for the
-- Bank: (i) shall be immune from legal process with respect to acts performed by them in their official capacity, except when the
-- Bank waives the immunity; (ii) where they are not local citizens or nationals, shall be accorded the same immunities from
-- immigration restrictions, alien registration requirements and national service obligations, and the same facilities as regards
-- exchange regulations, as are accorded by members to the representatives, officials and employees of comparable rank of other
-- members; and (iii) shall be granted the same treatment in respect of travelling facilities".
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `a Governor`
    `a Director`
    `an alternate`
    `an officer`
    `an employee`
    `an expert on a Bank mission`
    `a contractor supplying the Bank`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is Article 55 personnel` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a contractor supplying the Bank` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the act was in official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Bank has waived the immunity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is immune from legal process for the act` IF
        `the person is Article 55 personnel` `the person`
    AND `the act was in official capacity`
    AND (NOT `the Bank has waived the immunity`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the person is a local citizen or national` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person gets the immigration and national service immunities` IF
        `the person is Article 55 personnel` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person is a local citizen or national`)

§§ `Schedule, Article 56 and s 9(1) proviso -- taxation of the Bank`

-- Art 56(1): "The Bank, its assets, property, income and its operations and transactions, shall be exempt from all taxation and from
-- all customs duties. The Bank shall also be exempt from any obligation for the payment, withholding or collection of any tax or duty."
-- s 9(1) proviso: nothing in Article 56 shall be construed as "(a) entitling the Bank to import into Singapore goods free of any customs
-- duty without any restriction on their subsequent sale therein; (b) conferring on the Bank any exemption from taxes or duties which
-- form part of the price of goods sold; or (c) conferring on the Bank any exemption from taxes or duties which are in fact no more than
-- charges for services rendered."
-- The "sale restricted" import is read from (a): duty-free import is not excluded where the later sale IS restricted (inference from
-- the words "without any restriction").
DECLARE Levy IS ONE OF
    `income tax on the Bank's income`
    `customs duty on goods imported with a restriction on resale`
    `customs duty on goods imported with no restriction on resale`
    `a tax forming part of the price of goods sold to the Bank`
    `a charge for services rendered dressed as a tax`
    `a duty to withhold tax from the Bank's payments`
    `a tax on the Bank's transactions`

GIVEN `the levy` IS A Levy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Bank is exempt from the levy` IF
    CONSIDER `the levy`
    WHEN `customs duty on goods imported with no restriction on resale` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a tax forming part of the price of goods sold to the Bank` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a charge for services rendered dressed as a tax` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Schedule, Article 56(2) -- salaries paid by the Bank`

-- Art 56(2): "No tax shall be levied on or in respect of salaries and emoluments paid by the Bank to Directors, alternates, officers or
-- employees of the Bank, including experts performing missions for the Bank, except where a member deposits with its instrument of
-- ratification or acceptance a declaration that such member retains for itself and its political subdivisions the right to tax
-- salaries and emoluments paid by the Bank to citizens or nationals of such member."
-- Governors are named in Art 55 but NOT in Art 56(2); a contractor is in neither. The deposit does not say whether Singapore made the
-- declaration, so it is a parameter.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is named in Article 56(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a Governor` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a contractor supplying the Bank` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person,
      `the member made the retention declaration` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person is a citizen or national of that member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 56(2) bars tax on the Bank salary` IF
        `the person is named in Article 56(2)` `the person`
    AND (NOT (`the member made the retention declaration` AND `the person is a citizen or national of that member`))

§§ `Schedule, Article 56(3), (4) -- Bank bonds`

-- Art 56(3): no tax "of any kind" on any obligation or security ISSUED by the Bank, "including any dividend or interest thereon, by
-- whomsoever held: (i) which discriminates against such obligation or security solely because it is issued by the Bank; or (ii) if
-- the sole jurisdictional basis for such taxation is the place or currency in which it is issued, made payable or paid, or the location
-- of any office or place of business maintained by the Bank."
-- Art 56(4): the same for a security GUARANTEED by the Bank, but (ii) names only "the location of any office or place of business
-- maintained by the Bank" -- not the place or currency of issue or payment.
DECLARE Basis IS ONE OF
    `the holder's residence`
    `the place of issue`
    `the currency of issue`
    `the place of payment`
    `the location of a Bank office`

GIVEN `the basis` IS A Basis, `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the basis is a forbidden sole basis` IF
    CONSIDER `the basis`
    WHEN `the location of a Bank office` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the place of issue` THEN `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Bank`
    WHEN `the currency of issue` THEN `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Bank`
    WHEN `the place of payment` THEN `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Bank`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the basis` IS A Basis,
      `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Bank` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the basis is the sole jurisdictional basis` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the tax discriminates solely because of the Bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 56 bars the tax on the security` IF
        `the tax discriminates solely because of the Bank`
    OR  (`the basis is the sole jurisdictional basis` AND `the basis is a forbidden sole basis` `the basis` `the security is issued, not merely guaranteed, by the Bank`)
